    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A SemanticAdmissionCut is the seven-member tuple of claim c, claim judgment j_c, event e, event judgment j_e, materialized relation r, source frontier F_k and successor frontier F_k_plus_1. Its separate judgment j_a assesses the unchanged cut. These records retain distinct identities and authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 922,
          "quote": "RelationClaim c\n  -> Judgment j_c over unchanged c\n  -> candidate FrameworkEvent e binding c, j_c, and source frontier F_k\n  -> Judgment j_e over unchanged e\n  -> deterministic TypedRelation r materialized from (c, j_c, e, j_e, basis)\n  -> successor frontier F_k_plus_1\n  -> SemanticAdmissionCut a = (c, j_c, e, j_e, r, F_k, F_k_plus_1)\n  -> Judgment j_a over unchanged a",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FCandidate%2C%20Judgment%2C%20Event%2C%20And%20Relation%20Separation",
          "start_line": 915
        }
      ],
      "key": "semantic_admission_cut",
      "label": "Semantic admission cut"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The mutable-subject effect model distinguishes external reality W, stable SubjectBinding b_W, occurrence o_n, bounded observations q_n and q_n_plus_1, traversal classification F_K[v_n], separately identified domain operation op_n, executor, actor, owner-issued grant g_n, territory, immutable EffectInvocation, unchanged EffectSubject, readiness judgment, later EffectDisposition and TransitionSubject. The invocation binds occurrence, operation, executor, actor, grant, territory and inputs; the readiness subject binds occurrence, subject binding, pre-observation, invocation, operation, grant, territory and invalidation state.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1094,
          "quote": "F_K[v_n] classifies one traversal application.\nop_n is a separately identified domain operation.\ng_n is the exact owner-issued grant for op_n over b_W.\ninv_n = EffectInvocation(o_n, op_n, executor_n, actor_n, g_n, territory_n, inputs_n)\ns_n = EffectSubject(o_n, b_W, q_n, inv_n, op_n, g_n, territory_n, invalidation_n)\nj_ready = judge_effect_readiness(s_n)",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FMutable-Subject%20Effect%20Relation",
