    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The published semantic layer is the single constitutional truth surface of world-model work: published domain artifacts, bounded fragments, entity cuts, explicit treatments, covariance edges, adjoint mappings, temporal reference artifacts and composed world models built by reference. Epistemic overlays, query planes, mapping reports and compiled execution artifacts are supporting or downstream surfaces and create no second truth surface.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 588,
          "quote": "World-model work has one constitutional truth surface: the published semantic\nlayer.\n\nThat layer consists of:\n\n- published domain artifacts\n- their bounded fragments and published entity cuts\n- explicit treatments, covariance edges, adjoint mappings, and temporal\n  reference artifacts\n- composed world models built by reference from those published artifacts",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FSingle%20Truth%20Surface",
